agent_4.revised_operationalization:
1) Monthly biomass measurement and quota calculation;
2) Each fisher records their catch in the shared logbook;
3) At the monthly meeting the committee reviews the logbook, applies the redistribution formula, calculates and deducts the fine based on excess catch, updates each fisher’s reserve in the ledger, records any fines or assistance, and publishes the updated balances. If a fisher’s reserve is below 1 kg, the committee records the amount needed and ensures the community shares the required portion of the next catch.
4) If a fisher receives a small fish loan, the loan amount is recorded in the ledger. The fisher must pay back the loan in equal installments over the next three fishing seasons, with each installment no more than half of that season’s catch after keeping a 1 kg reserve. Any shortfall in an installment is carried forward to the next season. All loan repayments and remaining balances are logged transparently so every fisher can see their reserve status at any time.

